From 44b10d123956186264194bab20feab657b33659d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:11:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 61/82] sunxi: h713: say what the DDR3 path really does with
 tpr0..tpr2 at 636

Reading dram_sun50iw12.c for the 636 MHz case (brief F2a item 4) turned up one
wrong sentence in the comment this base was born with, inherited from
hy310_defconfig and from boards/hy300-pro/uboot.config: tpr0..tpr2 are not
"computed from the clock" on the DDR3 path. They are not read at all. The DDR3
arm of iw12_set_timing() builds DRAMC+0x02c..0x094 from a frozen cycle-count
table with four clock-scaled init timers; only the LPDDR3 arm unpacks
tpr0..tpr2 into register fields. Same outcome for the board -- the values are
inert either way -- but the reason matters to the next person who changes one
and wonders why nothing moved.

The reading found nothing wrong for 636 MHz, and the comment now says why. The
speed bin splits at 800 MHz, so 636 is in the low bin -- and so are the bench
board's 624 and, less obviously, the HY310's 792. The only branch that
separates the three is the PHY arm at clk > 672 in iw12_phy_train(), where 636
takes the same low side as the bench board's 624: the side verified
register-exact against that board's stock boot0, while 792 is the one that
crosses. 636 also falls inside the 312..1200 MHz sweep the DDR3 timing block
was generalised from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 configs/hy300_pro_defconfig | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig b/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig
index 538ecd598a8..40cfcaa50f9 100644
--- a/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig
+++ b/configs/hy300_pro_defconfig
@@ -26,9 +26,21 @@
 #     dump, which proves "enough for a dump", not "stable in operation".
 #   - tpr11/tpr12 0x44440000/0x00005555 are this board's, and differ from the
 #     HY310's 0x44340000/0x00006666.
-#   - tpr0..tpr2 are in the file for completeness only; the DDR3 path in
-#     arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50iw12.c recomputes them from CONFIG_DRAM_CLK
-#     and overwrites whatever is configured here.
+#   - tpr0..tpr2 are in the file for completeness only and have no effect:
+#     the DDR3 arm of iw12_set_timing() in
+#     arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50iw12.c never reads them. It builds
+#     DRAMC+0x02c..0x094 from a frozen cycle-count table plus four init
+#     timers scaled by the clock. Only the LPDDR3 arm unpacks tpr0..tpr2.
+#   - at 636 MHz nothing in the DDR3 path is new. Its speed bin splits at
+#     800 MHz, so this board is in the low bin -- CL/CWL 6/4, MR0 0x1c70,
+#     MR2 0x18, which is what this file happens to configure anyway (the
+#     path overrides mr0/mr2 itself and ignores the configured ones); so
+#     are the bench board's 624 and the HY310's 792. The one branch that
+#     does split the three is the PHY arm at clk > 672 in
+#     iw12_phy_train(): 636 takes the low side, exactly as the bench
+#     board's 624 does, and that is the side verified register-exact
+#     against that board's stock boot0. 636 also sits inside the
+#     312..1200 MHz sweep the DDR3 timing block was generalised from.
 #   - para2 and tpr13 are the values the vendor flash tool writes, as on a
 #     device.
 #   - the device tree is sun50i-h713-hy300-pro, an include of the bench board's
